.TH STEREO3DDEMO 1 "October 2026" "stereo3ddemo 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stereo3ddemo \- Stereo Demonstrator, 3D models in stereo with a 3D cursor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stereo3ddemo
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fImodel\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Stereo Demonstrator, by KDAB, shows 3D models (OBJ, FBX, glTF) on stereo displays with a 3D cursor drawn where the mouse meets the model, automatic focus over a focus area, asymmetric frusta, an eye separation taken from the focus distance, pop-out and the field of view from the screen's physical size.
.PP
This is the stereo version by Sparky Stereo OS: the 3D area is the one stereo surface, drawn with a quad-buffer OpenGL context where the stack gives one, or as the two eyes side by side declared to the desktop, which makes every screen's format from them.
The side menu holds the program's 3D options (Enable 3D, the stereo output path, the render resolution per eye, a shortcut to the display settings) and the demonstrator's own controls under Advanced.
Every setting is kept in
.IR ~/.config/stereo3ddemo/stereo3ddemo.conf .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I model
A model file to open (.obj, .fbx, .gltf, .glb). Without one the bundled motorbike is shown.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DISABLE_STEREO
When set, one picture is drawn and nothing is declared, as with Enable 3D off.
.TP
.B QT_LOGGING_RULES=stereo3ddemo.*=true
Logs the stereo path taken, the window's format, the declaration and the camera parameters.
.SH KEYS
F2 autofocus, F3 and F4 focus distance, F5 and F6 pop-out, F7 and F8 separation, F frustum overlay, W wireframe, C view all, Space cycles the cursor display mode, F11 full screen, F12 copies a screenshot to the clipboard.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Stereo Demonstrator: https://github.com/KDABLabs/stereo3ddemo
.br
The stereo version: https://github.com/Sparky-OS/stereo3ddemo
